per-backed stream storage, which the client doesn't need and which slow startup further. Publish port 6650 for the binary client protocol (serviceUrl pulsar://localhost:6650) and 8080 for the admin REST API. Use a fixed container name and remove any stale container in both @BeforeAll and @AfterAll, matching the existing rabbitmq test's cleanup pattern.\n\nRisks:\n- Standalone mode is heavier than the single-process brokers already allow-listed (rabbitmq, nats) — CI timeouts may need to be generous, and this adds real wall-clock cost per test run.\n- This is advisory: if the remaining dynamic-access classes the generator needs turn out to still be reachable without a live broker, the Docker setup adds cost without benefit — local Gradle/Native Image verification should confirm before committing to it.\n\nIteration progress:\n- Iteration: 1/3\n- Overall coverage: 422/989\n\nFull dynamic-access coverage report, all classes with uncovered call sites:\n### org.apache.pulsar.shade.io.netty.handler.ssl.util.OpenJdkSelfSignedCertGenerator\nSource: /home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata/forge/local_repositories/source_context/org.apache.pulsar/pulsar-client-all/4.2.5/main/extracted/org/apache/pulsar/shade/io/netty/handler/ssl/util/OpenJdkSelfSignedCertGenerator.java\nCoverage: 0/25\nUncovered call sites:\n- [reflection] java.lang.reflect.Constructor#newInstance(java.lang.Object[]) <- org.apache.pulsar.shade.io.netty.handler.ssl.util.OpenJdkSelfSignedCertGenerator.generate(OpenJdkSelfSignedCertGenerator.java:242) (line 242)\n- [reflection] java.lang.reflect.Constructor#newInstance(java.lang.Object[]) <- org.apache.pulsar.shade.io.netty.handler.ssl.util.OpenJdkSelfSignedCertGenerator.generate(OpenJdkSelfSignedCertGenerator.java:243) (line 243)\n- [reflection] java.lang.reflect.Constructor#newInstance(java.lang.Object[]) <- org.apache.pulsar.shade.io.netty.handler.ssl.util.OpenJdkSelfSignedCertGenerator.generate(OpenJdkSelfSignedCertGenerator.java:245) (line 245)\n- [r