SecurityValidator\", false,\n                    AvroTrustedClasses.class.getClassLoader());\n            return true;\n        } catch (ClassNotFoundException | LinkageError e) {\n            log.debug(\"Avro has no ClassSecurityValidator; trusted-class declarations are a no-op\");\n            return false;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private AvroTrustedClasses() {\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Everything declared through {@link AvroTrustedClasses}: the trusted names and predicates, and the\n     * record of which schemas have already been walked. One instance is live at a time and answers\n     * Avro's trust check; {@link AvroTrustedClasses#snapshot()} hands out a detached copy of it.\n     *\n     * <p>Opaque to callers, who only hold a copy and give it back to\n     * {@link AvroTrustedClasses#restore(State)}. Because that copy is detached, it is unaffected by\n     * anything declared afterwards and can be restored more than once.\n     */\n    public static final class State {\n\n        /** Trusted package prefixes; sub-packages are included. */\n        private final Set<String> trustedPackages = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n\n        /** Individually trusted binary class names. */\n        private final Set<String> trustedClasses = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n\n        /** Additional rules, for policies the name-based methods cannot express. */\n        private final Set<Predicate<Class<?>>> trustedPredicates = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n\n        /**\n         * Application classes whose derived schema has already been walked, so a class used for many\n         * producers or consumers is traversed once rather than on every schema construction. Holds\n         * names rather than Class objects, so it pins neither a class nor its loader.\n         */\n        private final Set<WalkKey> walked = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n\n        /**\n         * Identifies one traversal, by the schema that was walked rather than by the class alone. The\n         * same class can derive different schemas — JSR-310 conversions replace a named type with a\n         * logical primitive, and two class loaders can define different versions of the same class name\n         * — and each of those names a different set of types. Keying on the class alone could cache the\n         * smaller set and then refuse a type the larger one needs, which fails closed at serialization\n         * time. Holds names and schema text only, so it pins neither a class nor a loader.\n         */\n        private record WalkKey(String className, String schemaJson) {\n        }\n\n        private State() {\n        }\n\n        /** The built-in baseline: what a JVM starts out with before anything is declared. */\n        private static State withDefaults() {\n            State state = new State();\n            // Protobuf runtime types that avro-protobuf resolves when building a schema for a generated\n            // message, such as the com.google.protobuf.Any wrapper. Needed by Schema.PROTOBUF for any\n            // application, so it belongs to the client's own baseline rather than to a caller. In the\n            // shaded client this literal is relocated alongside the classes it names, so it still\n            // matches.\n            state.trustedPackages.add(\"com.google.protobuf\");\n            // Collection types that ReflectData records as a \"java-class\" property on the array or map\n            // schema it generates for a field, and then resolves reflectively. Trusting a class expands\n            // through the derived schema and picks these up on its own, but declaring a package or a\n            // bare class name does not, which made \"trust my model package\" quietly insufficient for\n            // any POJO with a List field. They are plain containers with nothing exploitable in\n            // construction, and Avro's own build trusts the same set, so there is no value in making\n            // callers rediscover them.\n            state.trustedClasses.addAll(Arrays.asList(\n                    \"java.util.Collection\",\n                    \"java.util.List\",\n                    \"java.util.ArrayList\",\n                    \"java.util.Set\",\n                    \"java.util.HashSet\",\n                    \"java.util.LinkedHashSet\",\n                    \"java.util.TreeSet\",\n                    \"java.util.Map\",\n                    \"java.util.HashMap\",\n                    \"java.util.LinkedHashMap\",\n                    \"java.util.TreeMap\",\n                    \"java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap\"));\n            return state;\n        }\n\n        /**\n         * An independent copy. Both {@code snapshot()} and {@code restore()} copy, so a copy handed to\n         * a caller never shares mutable state with the live instance.\n         */\n        private State copy() {\n            State copy = new State();\n            copy.trustedPackages.addAll(trustedPackages);\n            copy.trustedClasses.addAll(trustedClasses);\n            copy.trustedPredicates.addAll(trustedPredicates);\n            copy.walked.addAll(walked);\n            return copy;\n        }\n\n        private void addClassName(String className) {\n            if (className != null && !className.isEmpty()) {\n                trustedClasses.add(className);\n            }\n        }\n\n        private void addClassNames(Collection<String> classNames) {\n            for (String className : classNames) {\n                addClassName(className);\n            }\n        }\n\n        private void addPackageNames(Collection<String> packageNames) {\n            for (String packageName : packageNames) {\n                if (packageName != null && !packageName.isEmpty()) {\n                    trustedPackages.add(packageName);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        private void addPredicate(Predicate<Class<?>> predicate) {\n            trustedPredicates.add(predicate);\n        }\n\n        /** Records a traversal, returning false when this schema has already been walked. */\n        private boolean markWalked(String className, String schemaJson) {\n            return walked.add(new WalkKey(className, schemaJson));\n        }\n\n        private int walkedCount() {\n            return walked.size();\n\n[421 more lines in file. Use offset=260 to continue.]"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1792426638381}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_BcB9DvK6MKkR1F5k1julNW19|fc_0bf7130f74ebe3a8016ad6428de30c87d1a3bbb2fbd880bb3b", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "/*\n * Copyright and related rights waived via CC0\n *\n * You should have received a copy of the CC0 legalcode along with this\n * work. If not, see <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/>.\n */\npackage org_apache_pulsar.pulsar_client_all;\n\nimport static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;\n\nimport org.apache.pulsar.client.schema.AvroTrustedClasses;\nimport org.apache.pulsar.shade.org.apache.avro.Protocol;\nimport org.apache.pulsar.shade.org.apache.avro.Schema;\nimport org.apache.pulsar.shade.org.apache.avro.generic.GenericData.InstanceSupplier;\nimport org.apache.pulsar.shade.org.apache.avro.specific.SpecificData;\nimport org.apache.pulsar.shade.org.apache.avro.specific.SpecificRecordBase;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\n\npublic class SpecificDataTest {\n    @Test\n    void readsGeneratedModelSchemaAndProtocolFields() {\n        SpecificData model = SpecificData.getForClass(GeneratedRecord.class);\n        Schema schema = SpecificData.get().getSchema(GeneratedRecord.class);\n        Protocol protocol = SpecificData.get().getProtocol(GeneratedService.class);\n\n        assertThat(model).isSameAs(GeneratedRecord.MODEL$);\n        assertThat(schema.getType()).isEqualTo(Schema.Type.RECORD);\n        assertThat(schema.getName()).isEqualTo(\"GeneratedRecord\");\n        assertThat(protocol.getMessages()).containsKey(\"lookup\");\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    void constructsSpecificRecordsAndUsesCachedInstanceSupplier() {\n        synchronized (AvroTrustedClasses.class) {\n            AvroTrustedClasses.State previousTrust = AvroTrustedClasses.snapshot();\n            AvroTrustedClasses.trustExactly(GeneratedRecord.class);\n            try {\n                SchemaConstructedRecord constructed = (SchemaConstructedRecord) SpecificData.newInstance(\n                        SchemaConstructedRecord.class, SchemaConstructedRecord.SCHEMA$);\n                InstanceSupplier supplier = SpecificData.get().getNewRecordSupplier(GeneratedRecord.SCHEMA$);\n                Object supplied = supplier.newInstance(null, GeneratedRecord.SCHEMA$);\n\n                assertThat(constructed.constructorSchema).isSameAs(SchemaConstructedRecord.SCHEMA$);\n                assertThat(supplied).isInstanceOf(GeneratedRecord.class);\n                assertThat(supplier.newInstance(supplied, GeneratedRecord.SCHEMA$)).isSameAs(supplied);\n            } finally {\n                AvroTrustedClasses.restore(previousTrust);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    public interface GeneratedService {\n        Protocol PROTOCOL = Protocol.parse(\"\"\"\n                {\n                  \"protocol\": \"GeneratedService\",\n                  \"namespace\": \"org_apache_pulsar.pulsar_client_all\",\n                  \"messages\": {\n                    \"lookup\": {\n                      \"request\": [{\"name\": \"key\", \"type\": \"string\"}],\n                      \"response\": \"string\"\n                    }\n                  }\n                }\n                \"\"\");\n    }\n\n    public static class GeneratedRecord extends SpecificRecordBase {\n        public static final Schema SCHEMA$ = new Schema.Parser().parse(\"\"\"\n                {\n                  \"type\": \"record\",\n                  \"name\": \"GeneratedRecord\",\n                  \"namespace\": \"org_apache_pulsar.pulsar_client_all.SpecificDataTest\",\n                  \"fields\": []\n                }\n                \"\"\");\n        public static final SpecificData MODEL$ = new SpecificData();\n\n        public GeneratedRecord() {\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public Schema getSchema() {\n            return SCHEMA$;\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public Object get(int field) {\n            throw new IndexOutOfBoundsException(\"field \" + field);\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public void put(int field, Object value) {\n            throw new IndexOutOfBoundsException(\"field \" + field);\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static class SchemaConstructedRecord extends SpecificRecordBase\n            implements SpecificData.SchemaConstructable {\n        public static final Schema SCHEMA$ = new Schema.Parser().parse(\"\"\"\n                {\n                  \"type\": \"record\",\n                  \"name\": \"SchemaConstructedRecord\",\n                  \"namespace\": \"org_apache_pulsar.pulsar_client_all.SpecificDataTest\",\n                  \"fields\": []\n                }\n                \"\"\");\n        private final Schema constructorSchema;\n\n        public SchemaConstructedRecord(Schema schema) {\n            constructorSchema = schema;\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public Schema getSchema() {\n            return SCHEMA$;\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public Object get(int field) {\n            throw new IndexOutOfBoundsException(\"field \" + field);\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public void put(int field, Object value) {\n            throw new IndexOutOfBoundsException(\"field \" + field);\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1792426638382}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_7vYPGyJe989xtFbsmPpXj7Jv|fc_0bf7130f74ebe3a8016ad6428de31887d19efd67e69fe53281", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "/*\n * Copyright and related rights waived via CC0\n *\n * You should have received a copy of the CC0 legalcode along with this\n * work. If not, see <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/>.\n */\npackage org_apache_pulsar.pulsar_client_all;\n\nimport static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;\n\nimport java.lang.reflect.Type;\nimport java.lang.reflect.TypeVariable;\nimport org.apache.pulsar.shade.com.google.common.reflect.TypeResolver;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\n\npublic class TypesInnerTypeVariableInvocationHandlerTest {\n    @Test\n    void resolvesDependentBoundsThroughSyntheticTypeVariable() {\n        TypeVariable<?>[] variables = Dependent.class.getTypeParameters();\n        Type resolved = new TypeResolver()\n                .where(variables[0], String.class)\n                .resolveType(variables[1]);\n\n        assertThat(resolved).isInstanceOf(TypeVariable.class);\n        TypeVariable<?> resolvedVariable = (TypeVariable<?>) resolved;\n        assertThat(resolvedVariable.getName()).isEqualTo(\"U\");\n        assertThat(resolvedVariable.getBounds()).containsExactly(String.class);\n    }\n\n    private static final class Dependent<T, U extends T> {\n    }\n}\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1792426638382}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_Xls2CE0GZJrKlkL5zm8fxpKI|fc_0bf7130f74ebe3a8016ad6428de32087d1b8cec58fda3bbe26", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "/*\n * Copyright and related rights waived via CC0\n *\n * You should have received a copy of the CC0 legalcode along with this\n * work. If not, see <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/>.\n */\npackage org_apache_pulsar.pulsar_client_all;\n\nimport static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;\n\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport org.apache.pulsar.shade.io.netty.util.Version;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\n\npublic class VersionTest {\n    @Test\n    void discoversBundledNettyBuildMetadata() {\n        Map<String, Version> versions = Version.identify();\n\n        assertThat(versions).isNotEmpty();\n        assertThat(versions.values()